Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin (@em-staelin: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC
David H. Staelin. Electromagnetics and Applications, preliminary text, copyright 2011; preface dated 5 January 2011. [MIT 6.013 readings](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-013-electromagnetics-and-applications-spring-2009/pages/readings/) · [Complete text](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-013-electromagnetics-and-applications-spring-2009/d3be4ea78b036a6362230fb41780cf54_MIT6_013S09_notes.pdf).

Study all thirteen chapters, reconstruct worked applications and solve substantial exercises. The text connects Maxwell fields with circuits, transmission, forces, devices, waves, radiation and optical systems. Use the associated complete 6.013 course for a second engineering progression.

The course run is Spring 2009; the linked text's copyright is 2011. Front matter and contents were inspected on 29 October 2026. OCW's general CC BY-NC-SA terms have exceptions; identify the actual book's permissions notice rather than transferring the site's licence to every component. All files remain external references.

